So, Kathie the knight ascended.

I thought I'd already ascended a knight, then I realized that I couldn't 
find either the entry in my logfile nor my ascension notes, so perhaps I 
hadn't. So. Now I have. Though since I've been playing Tourists and 
Healers lately, a Knight without conducts was kind of anticlimactic.

This was a standard game, nothing special. Sokoban was the amulet, a 
random BoH appeared in the Mines, and Mines End was the old one where 
the gems are cached in closets. Minetown altar was cross-aligned, and 
Minetown had a bones file. The bones loot was nothing spectacular but it 
did let me buy another point of protection.

I set up camp at a coaligned altar on DL8, below Sokoban. A very few 
sacrifices gave me Sunsword. 

Maybe two DLs later was a two-ghost bones level with bags of holding 
(cursed) and assorted loot, and I'd found a random !HW to get at least 
one of the BoHs uncursed and looted, and got Magicbane (which of course 
I couldn't use) and Mojo (ditto), plus assorted cursed magic armor which 
I couldn't uncurse yet. 

A long sacrificing session gave me Grayswandir and got me crowned. Even 
with extreme luck and all that, though, I ran through 9 bl?ID trying to 
get a full pack ID. 

MR came from the scales of a grey dragon in Ludios. Quest was easier 
than I expected (but how does a D curse your stuff?). Castle wand 
started at 0:2 and I never used it. The castle throne gave me a wish, 
and I decided that since it came so easily perhaps I didn't need this 
one to be wishless and I got a =FA which it turned out I'd already had, 
unidentified.

This was the first time I played smart enough to really use cursed?TP: 
>From VoD to the bottom (DL 48 in this dungeon), then I mapped my way 
back up to VoD (had three markers from bones and randomly generated, 
plus wished from Vlad's throne for a fourth, so marker charges weren't 
an issue; I never recharged any of the markers) and took out Vlad on the 
way up. After a final session of polypiling, blanking, and alchemy back 
at VoD I had 40 bl!FH; it's amazing how many of these things show up 
when you're using a weapon that doesn't destroy potions. And then it 
turned out that !FH were smoky, and I got two more wishes drinking the 
20 or so potions that I couldn't carry to the End Game. I asked for tins 
of tengu meat, but neither tin gave me intrinsic TC to go with the 
teleportitis I'd had since a random hostile tengu appeared (and was 
killed and eaten, of course) on the Quest. I had =TC, but I was hoping 
to save the ring slot for =SD. 

My wand of Death missed Rodney twice when I went to get the Book of the 
Dead. Lovely. But otherwise, the run down to Moloch's then back up was 
textbook. I used c!GL to get out of Moloch's, had all of Gehennom mapped 
and dug, didn't have a terrible time being dragged backwards, and only 
saw Rodney on DL 41 (Orcus town) and the VoD. The wand worked the first 
time for the reappearances.

On Astral, Pestilence was heading for me when I first arrived. Since I 
had to deal with it anyway, I went first to its altar, on the left: 
Chaotic. Backed back out and headed up the middle, where Pestilence 
reappeared (huh?) with Famine, but the altar was Neutral. Got sickened 
once by Pestilence as I headed toward Death's side, on the right, for 
the Lawful altar; the unihorn fixed the sickness. (Is it normal for the 
"sickened" thing on the status line to be off-screen? I wasn't sure I 
was sick until I cured [unihorned] myself.)

And a choir sang and all that.

